# Apple signing material. EAS generates and stores this for us, but any of it
# can also land here — `eas credentials` writes credentials.json, and Apple
# hands out .p8 keys and .p12 certificates if you ever manage signing by hand.
# None of it belongs in a repository, and this list is also what keeps it off
# the EAS build servers: `eas build` packages the project by .gitignore, so an
# ignored file is one that never leaves this machine.
credentials.json
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest

